  "title": "Multi-agent patterns in VS Code you won't learn from docs",
  "description": "Building with one agent is familiar. Orchestrating a fleet of them in parallel across local, background, and cloud surfaces is where it gets real. You'll see the decisions that matter, how to decompose work across agents, when to fork vs. delegate, and how to verify quality when agents outnumber you. Leave with patterns for multi-agent workflows you can apply to your own codebase tomorrow.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
